And around it, then, of poplars nourished-by-water was a grove,
all round, circular, and down cold flowed water
from on high out of the rock;

There them met the son of Dolius, Melanthius,
goats driving, which among all the herds of goats were outstanding,
as a meal for the suitors;

“Nymphs of the spring, daughters of Zeus, if ever Odysseus
for you thigh-pieces burned, having covered them in rich fat,
of lambs and of kids, this wish for me fulfil,

And close by, Odysseus and the heavenly swineherd
stood still, as they came, and about them came the sound
of the hollow lyre;

From others, others are, and has been fitted out for it the courtyard
with a wall and with copings, and the doors well-fenced are,
folding;
